      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-4{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=5{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=-3{b}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =8{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2}+3{b}_{3} \\\\  & =3{b}_{3}+8{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(-4{b}_{3})+\\frac{8}{5}(5{b}_{1})+\\frac{2}{3}(-3{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}{c}_{1}+\\frac{8}{5}{c}_{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{8}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].$",
